            {
                "entry_id": "b3e4bb7d-b987-3dd7-b77c-b94763618e7d",
                "word": "incognito",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0da241a8-0d32-4c21-9799-30833b39bd20",
                        "entry_id": "b3e4bb7d-b987-3dd7-b77c-b94763618e7d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "incognitos"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "58fdf521-f781-34d0-8341-313eebb0ec10",
                        "entry_id": "b3e4bb7d-b987-3dd7-b77c-b94763618e7d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One unknown or in disguise, or under an assumed character or name."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c75e422c-1c4e-3cc8-b98e-e96433d9a2c1",
                        "entry_id": "b3e4bb7d-b987-3dd7-b77c-b94763618e7d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The assumption of disguise or of a feigned character; the state of being in disguise or not recognized."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f5caa18-aa2e-409e-a7d3-baa79dc9e33f",
                                "sense_id": "c75e422c-1c4e-3cc8-b98e-e96433d9a2c1",
                                "text": "Of those letters, and other attempts of the same kind, the author could not complain, though his incognito was endangered. He had challenged the public to a game at bo-peep, and if he was discovered in his “hiding-hole,” he must submit to the shame of detection."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46324590-2086-4de0-b3c6-0c7fccddc8ba",
                                "sense_id": "c75e422c-1c4e-3cc8-b98e-e96433d9a2c1",
                                "text": "It contained a letter from the King himself, craving hospitality for a few days, as his mother was about to visit England, and to take up with Lord Avonleigh her residence at the Castle. A slight incognito would be preserved, and as little form and ceremony expected as was possible."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
